<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">University of San Carlos of Guatemala</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1676</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as USAC</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The University of San Carlos of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guatemala">Guatemala</a> is the country's oldest and only public university, founded by royal decree in 1676 in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santiago">Santiago</a> de los Caballeros, today <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antigua-guatemala">Antigua Guatemala</a>, and later moved to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guatemala-city">Guatemala City</a>. Granted autonomy by the revolutionary government in 1944–1945, it became a centre of political opposition, and many of its students and teachers were killed during the civil war.</p></div>
